# Generated outputs
figures/
runs/
results/
_nb_results/

# _results/ is generated too (~115 MB: figures, pooled-query CSVs, model
# zips) and stays out of git -- EXCEPT the two small text files that are
# inputs to a later analysis stage rather than just outputs:
#
#   regret_test.json        solo terminal SR per agent; thread-a reads it to
#                           pick its best-solo reference and build the
#                           inverse-regret weights.
#   correlation_trained.csv thread-a's independence weights come from this.
#
# ~12 KB total, and versioning them means `git log` explains why a figure's
# numbers moved. It also means `git pull` delivers them to the cluster, so
# the thread array jobs need no separate file transfer.
#
# Re-including files under an ignored directory needs the directory itself
# un-ignored first, hence the /* + negation pattern rather than `_results/`.
_results/*
!_results/*/
_results/*/*
!_results/*/regret_test.json
!_results/*/correlation_trained.csv

# The manuscript source itself -- plain text, and the one file here that is
# authored rather than generated. Its build products (.pdf/.aux/.out/
# .synctex.gz) stay ignored by the rule above.
!_results/story.tex

